{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>As was done on this day.</b> Meaning: just as Moses did on this day, so HaShem commanded to do for the seven days of ordination. It should properly have been כאשר עשיתי, but such is the way of the sacred language, like והי׳ יחזקאל לכם, and similarly ואת יפתח ואת שמואל. Proof that the meaning is HaShem commanded to do thus: ועשית לאהרן ולבניו ככה ככל אשר צויתי אותכם שבעת ימים, and further: ופר חטאת תעשה ליום, like שנים ליום עולה תמיד, and it is written there וחטאת על המזבח ומשחת אותו בכל יום until the end of the ordination, and further: שבעת ימים תכפר על המזבח. He did not mention the two rams because he took a shortcut, and many hold that only the bull of sin-offering is made each day; in my opinion, the reason he mentions the bull is because blood of the ram of burnt-offering is applied upon Aaron and his sons, and the second ram — its flesh is eaten, whereas only the bull of sin-offering effects atonement upon the altar, and similarly written concerning atonements, its meaning being on account of atonements."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:11.174212283Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}